// PORT-PENDING 1030 tests-determinism-module-group: tests/determinism.rs:1-765
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-DET1 (ratified 2026-06-22): `#Pure` ⇒ reproducible.
//RS //!
//RS //! Two ratified pieces beyond the base purity checks (which already ship as
//RS //! E3401/E3403):
//RS //!   1. Injected deterministic `Clock` / `Rng` capabilities — a `#Pure fn` may
//RS //!      read time/randomness THROUGH a `Clock`/`Rng` parameter (seeded by the
//RS //!      caller, hence reproducible), while ambient `time.now()`/`random.int()`
//RS //!      stay E3403.
//RS //!   2. `#Nondeterministic("reason") { … }` — expert escape suspending
//RS //!      determinism rejections (E3401/E3403) for its body.
//RS //!
//RS //! #2515 HashMap census for the native build path: `native_effect_projection`
//RS //! orders `summaries.values()` before authority rows reach receipts or
//RS //! diagnostics; `dependency_interface_fingerprint` sorts its `dep_roots`
//RS //! results before key hashing; Loader boundary policies and package dependency
//RS //! diagnostics are sorted before they reach emitted diagnostics. RuntimeCache
//RS //! identity and Driver symbol maps are lookup-only and have no output iteration.
//RS 
//RS mod common;
//RS 
//RS // ── Piece 1: injected deterministic Clock / Rng ───────────────────────────────
//RS 
