// PORT-PENDING 1030 tests-determinism-module-group: tests/dev.rs:1-30
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! E2-M4 — `jet dev` interpreter tests: the routine slice.
//RS //!
//RS //! The crux is the **differential battery** (D-DEV, I2): for each supported
//RS //! program, the interpreter's stdout/stderr/exit code MUST be byte-for-byte
//RS //! identical to the compiled native binary. Any divergence is a P0
//RS //! miscompile-class bug — the interpreter is a dev convenience that must never
//RS //! lie about what the real build does. This mirrors `tests/comptime_diff.rs`.
//RS //!
//RS //! Also tested here:
//RS //!   - canonical evaluator terminal diagnostics (E0956/E2202),
//RS //!   - the per-iteration `dev_iteration` function the watch loop is built on.
//RS //!
//RS //! The D-DEV3 save-to-diagnostic latency budget is NOT here: a wall-clock
//RS //! verdict cannot be taken inside a parallel suite, so #2005 moved it to
//RS //! `tests/dev_latency.rs`.
//RS //!
//RS //! #2020: the whole-corpus batteries are NOT here. One binary could not run its
//RS //! own 165 declared tests inside the 900s suite guard, so the corpus batteries
//RS //! moved to sibling targets — `dev_interp_parity`, `dev_default_parity`,
//RS //! `dev_tier_parity`, `dev_corpus`, `dev_corpus_gate` — each with its own budget.
//RS //! Every one of them is a `tests/*.rs` file, so cargo builds a binary for each;
//RS //! `tests/suites.txt` then puts each one in a named verification set and
//RS //! `tests/suite_membership.rs` fails if any declared target is in none (#2025).
//RS //! `Tools/ci/test-shards.sh` shards the whole inventory (D-CI1=A).
//RS //! `every_dev_slice_is_wired_into_a_test_target` pins that nothing was dropped.
//RS #![allow(dead_code, unused_imports)]
//RS 
//RS mod common;
//RS include!("dev_parts/support.rs");
//RS include!("dev_parts/routine.rs");
// END-PORT-PENDING 1030 tests/dev.rs:1-30

